## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design privacy-preserving, cross-account audit trails in a multi-tenant AWS environment, ensuring complete isolation between tenants while maintaining compliance and enabling proper access controls.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-account CloudTrail organization-level centralization
- Per-tenant Data Events scoped to approved services only
- PII redaction during log ingestion
- Fine-grained access control with Lake Formation or IAM policies
- Automated tenant onboarding and offboarding workflows
- Secure querying mechanisms with tenant isolation
- Rollback strategies for configuration changes

## Code Example

```javascript
exports.handler = async (evt) => {
  const rec = JSON.parse(evt.Records[0].Sns.Message);
  const piiFields = ['userIdentity', 'recipientAccountId', 'session'];
  const redact = (obj) => {
    for (const key in obj) {
      if (piiFields.includes(key)) obj[key] = '[REDACTED]';
      if (typeof obj[key] === 'object') redact(obj[key]);
    }
  };
  redact(rec);
  return rec;
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of ephemeral cross‑account access, least privilege, VPC endpoints, and auditability. It also probes revocation semantics for temporary credentials.

## Key Concepts
- STS AssumeRole with session duration
- Cross‑account IAM roles and trust policies
- S3 bucket policies with resource and condition constraints
- VPC Endpoint restrictions
- CloudTrail auditing
- Revocation mechanics for temporary credentials

## Code Example
```javascript
// trust policy example (role in data owner account)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::PARTNER_AWS_ACCOUNT:role/PartnerDataAccess"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"sts:ExternalId": "data-exchange-2026"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
// bucket policy snippet (only for the assumed role and specific VPC endpoint)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::PARTNER_AWS_ACCOUNT:role/PartnerDataAccess"},
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::partner-data-bucket",
        "arn:aws:s3:::partner-data-bucket/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:SourceVpce": "vpce-EXAMPLE"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

